refore, the function $y={e}^{-4x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y={e}^{4x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4{e}^{4x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4y \\\\ 4{e}^{4x} & =4{e}^{4x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y={e}^{4x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=4{e}^{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4{e}^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4y \\\\ 4{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}4(4{e}^{x}) \\\\ 4{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}16{e}^{x} \\\\ 0 & \\ne 12{e}^{x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=4{e}^{x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/state.json" "file_sha256" "8369cbef007ac0b1b5e792706dd6fc6da36f26f34c6c22a9f09c822e89035f0c"} {"question" "q-79330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "61ab82ea09638a682d295b0b902655b36e516e962c6bc61f8eb430cccffc20f7"} {"question" "q-79330" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/state.json" "file_sha256" "8369cbef007ac0b1b5e792706dd6fc6da36f26f34c6c22a9f09c822e89035f0c"} {"question" "q-79330" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I on