ext{d}x}=10{x}^{9}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{5y}{x} \\\\ 10{x}^{9} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5({x}^{10})}{x} \\\\ 10{x}^{9} & \\overset{?}{=}5{x}^{9} \\\\ 5{x}^{9} & \\ne 0.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y={x}^{10}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=5{x}^{4},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=20{x}^{3}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{5y}{x} \\\\ 20{x}^{3} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5(5{x}^{4})}{x} \\\\ 20{x}^{3} & \\overset{?}{=}25{x}^{3} \\\\ 0 & \\ne 5{x}^{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=5{x}^{4}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/state.json" "file_sha256" "8369cbef007ac0b1b5e792706dd6fc6da36f26f34c6c22a9f09c822e89035f0c"} {"question" "q-141101" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "61ab82ea09638a682d295b0b902655b36e516e962c6bc61f8eb430cccffc20f7"} {"question" "q-141101" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/state.json" "file_sha256" "8369cbef007ac0b1b5e792706dd6fc6da36f26f34c6c22a9f09c822e89035f0c"} {"question" "q-141101" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/state.json" "file_sha256" "8369cbef007ac0b1b5e792706dd6fc6da36f26f34c6c22a9f09c822e89035f0c"} {"question" "q-141101" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/state.json" "file_sha256" "8369cbef007ac0b1b5e792706dd6fc6da36f26f34c6c22a9f09c822e89035f0c"} {"question" "q-141113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{2y}{x},\\,y(2)=-1.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/state.json" "file_sha256" "8369cbef007ac0b1b5e792706dd6fc6da36f26f34c6c22a9f09c822e89035f0c"} {"question" "q-141113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We're given that $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(2)=-1.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(2)=-1$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{A}{{2}^{2}} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{A}{4} \\\\ A & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/state.json" "file_sha256" "8369cbef007ac0b1b5e792706dd6fc6da36f26f34c6c22a9f09c822e89035f0c"} {"question" "q-141113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "61ab82ea09638a682d295b0b902655b36e516e962c6bc61f8eb430cccffc20f7"} {"question" "q-141113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/state.json" "file_sha256" "8369cbef007ac0b1b5e792706dd6fc6da36f26f34c6c22a9f09c822e89035f0c"} {"question" "q-141113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/state.json" "file_sha256" "8369cbef007ac0b1b5e792706dd6fc6da36f26f34c6c22a9f09c822e89035f0c"} {"question" "q-141113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/state.json" "file_sha256" "8369cbef007ac0b1b5e792706dd6fc6da36f26f34c6c22a9f09c822e89035f0c"} {"question" "q-141114" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{y}{x},\\,y(-1)=3.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=Ax$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/state.json" "file_sha256" "8369cbef007ac0b1b5e792706dd6fc6da36f26f34c6c22a9f09c822e89035f0c"} {"question" "q-141114" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We're given that $y=Ax$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(-1)=3.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(-1)=3$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =Ax \\\\ 3 & =A(-1) \\\\ 3 & =-A \\\\ A & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-3x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/state.json" "file_sha256" "8369cbef007ac0b1b5e792706dd6fc6da36f26f34c6c22a9f09c822e89035f0c"} {"question" "q-141114" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "61ab82ea09638a682d295b0b902655b36e516e962c6bc61f8eb430cccffc20f7"} {"question" "q-141114" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/state.json" "file_sha256" "8369cbef007ac0b1b5e792706dd6fc6da36f26f34c6c22a9f09c822e89035f0c"} {"question" "q-141114" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/state.json" "file_sha256" "8369cbef007ac0b1b5e792706dd6fc6da36f26f34c6c22a9f09c822e89035f0c"} {"question" "q-141114" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/state.json" "file_sha256" "8369cbef007ac0b1b5e792706dd6fc6da36f26f34c6c22a9f09c822e89035f0c"} {"question" "q-352654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3y,\\,y(2)=5.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=A{e}^{3x}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$\n\n$A=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/state.json" "file_sha256" "8369cbef007ac0b1b5e792706dd6fc6da36f26f34c6c22a9f09c822e89035f0c"} {"question" "q-352654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We're given that $y=A{e}^{3x}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(2)=5.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(2)=5$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =A{e}^{3x} \\\\ 5 & =A{e}^{3\\cdot 2} \\\\ 5 & =A{e}^{6} \\\\ \\frac{5}{{e}^{6}} & =A \\\\ A & =\\frac{5}{{e}^{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/state.json" "file_sha256" "8369cbef007ac0b1b5e792706dd6fc6da36f26f34c6c22a9f09c822e89035f0c"} {"question" "q-352654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062226/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "61ab82ea09638a682d295b0b902655b36e516e962c6bc61f8eb430cccffc20f7"} {"question" "q-352654" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Acad